                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "The original PvZ remains a masterclass in tower defense design, striking a near-flawless balance between approachable casual play and genuine strategic depth. Its charming aesthetic, clever environmental modifiers (like fog, pool, and roof stages), and iconic soundtrack give it timeless personality. While the campaign leans on the easy side for seasoned strategy veterans, the escalating challenge of Survival Mode and mini-games keeps it endlessly replayable. It’s a pure, microtransaction-free classic that still holds up brilliantly today.\n\n[b]RATING: 9/10[/b]",
